 {
  "coord": "32:0",
  "verdict": "FAIL",
  "category": "invention",
  "note": "Adds \"he said\" and turns \"unwilling to acknowledge\" into \"could not\"; \"She had given reasons\" dropped.",
  "replacement": "Mr. Pontellier heard that his wife intended to abandon her home and set up house elsewhere. He answered at once with a letter of unqualified disapproval and remonstrance. She had given reasons that he was unwilling to acknowledge as adequate. He hoped she had not yet acted on her rash impulse, and he begged her to consider first, foremost and above all else what people would say. In warning her he was not dreaming of scandal, which would never have crossed his mind in connection with his wife’s name or his own. He was thinking simply of his financial integrity. Word might get around that the Pontelliers had met with reverses and had to run their ménage on a humbler scale than before. That might do incalculable mischief to his business prospects."
 },
